# Extension Manifest & Packaging Guardrails

Xtract Replies is a Manifest V3 Chrome Extension that extracts replies from X.com posts into CSV/HTML.

## Manifest V3 Requirements

- **Service Worker**: `background.js` owns extraction state (`chrome.storage.session`), toolbar badge, and messaging between the content script and `popup.html`.
- **Permissions**: Include `"storage"` whenever using `chrome.storage.*`. Guard session storage access so a missing API never crashes SW registration.
- **Toolbar popup only**: Prefer `action.default_popup` + `chrome.action.openPopup()` from the service worker in the same turn as an in-page click. Do **not** open results with `chrome.windows.create` (Chrome blocks that as a popup without a transferable user gesture).
- **Host Permissions**: Include `https://x.com/*` and `https://www.instagram.com/*`.
- **Content Scripts**: `main.js` on `https://x.com/*/status/*`; `instagram.js` on `https://www.instagram.com/*`. Both use `run_at: "document_idle"`.
- **Web Accessible Resources**: `assets/icon.svg` and `assets/48.png` accessible on `https://x.com/*` and `https://www.instagram.com/*`.

## Version Syncing & Release Packaging

1. **Version Sync**:
   - Whenever updating `version` in `package.json`, run `npm run sync-version` to update `manifest.json`.
2. **Packaging**:
   - Run `npm run pack` to generate `xtract-replies-{version}.zip`.
   - Pack only runtime files (`manifest.json`, scripts, popup, assets, LICENSE, README, PRIVACY). Exclude `.cursor/`, workspace files, `graphics/`, and source `.zip` files.

```bash
npm run sync-version
npm run pack
```
